  faqs: [
    { question: "Where would my family in Nagercoil even find a genuine IB tutor?", answer: "Start by telling IB Gram your child's exact programme, subject and level; since Kanyakumari district has no local IB school, we shortlist tutors on syllabus experience gathered from across the country rather than location. Lesson timing gets fixed around your household only after that, and a free trial lesson happens before anything is agreed. If the first tutor is not the right fit, another one steps in." },
    { question: "Is a Cambridge or Edexcel IGCSE tutor available for a Nagercoil student?", answer: "Yes, for either board. Tutoring follows whichever specification, Cambridge or Edexcel, your child has actually chosen, delivered entirely online since neither runs at a school inside the district. Matching happens by exact code and tier, whether that is Extended Mathematics 0580 or Chemistry 0620, using that board's genuine past papers and mark schemes." },
    { question: "Do tutors actually travel out to a family's home in Nagercoil?", answer: "No, they do not. House visits are limited to Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR; everywhere else, Nagercoil included, a lesson happens live online, one to one, over video with a shared whiteboard. That counts as real tuition from home, just without anyone physically arriving there." },
    { question: "What's a realistic cost for IB or IGCSE tutoring based in Nagercoil?", answer: "The rate depends on the programme, subject and level, session length, and how recently a tutor has taught that specific syllabus, confirmed for your particular match before the trial begins. Diploma HL subjects usually cost more than Cambridge IGCSE Core support does. Since every session runs online, travel adds nothing to the fee, and there is no fixed contract to worry about." },
    { question: "Is there any school in Nagercoil that actually teaches IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Not currently. Schools such as Scott Christian Higher Secondary School and Carmel Higher Secondary School, along with most others across the district, follow Tamil Nadu's State Board, Matriculation Board, CBSE or ICSE. A family after an IB or Cambridge/Edexcel qualification either boards a child outside Kanyakumari district or builds it through tutoring while staying enrolled locally." },
    { question: "My daughter boards outside Tamil Nadu at an IB school. Can holiday tutoring work around that?", answer: "It regularly does, and it's a common reason Nagercoil families reach out, given that no local school runs the Diploma or Middle Years Programme. Tutors get matched to the precise subject, level and syllabus the boarding school follows, with sessions scheduled around holiday dates or, where the school allows it, an agreed evening slot during term." },
    { question: "Can we see how a tutor teaches before agreeing to anything?", answer: "Yes, every match includes a free trial lesson first. Your child works through a genuine topic from their own syllabus live online, with nothing charged and no obligation attached. A short plan for the first month follows, which you can approve, send back for changes, or set aside in favour of a different tutor." },
    { question: "Would a tutor ever write part of an Internal Assessment for a Nagercoil student?", answer: "That is one line IB Gram will not cross. A tutor can help narrow down a research question worth pursuing, walk through what a criterion is genuinely rewarding, sanity-check a data-collection plan and mark up a draft honestly, but the words on the page stay the student's, because anything else falls foul of the IB's own rules on academic honesty." },
    { question: "Which Diploma subjects can a Nagercoil family get tutoring in?", answer: "Most requests land on one of the two Maths routes, Physics, Chemistry or Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A or Computer Science, and the core trio of TOK, the Extended Essay and CAS reflection that every Diploma student carries regardless of subject choice." },
    { question: "Does tutoring cover MYP and PYP too, or only the Diploma?", answer: "Yes, tutoring spans the whole continuum for Nagercoil families, whether a child is enrolled at an IB school elsewhere or picking up a curriculum fresh. Younger MYP students work on criterion-graded analysis across sciences and languages and on the Personal Project; PYP sessions build reading confidence, number sense and the inquiry habits an Exhibition later draws on." },
    { question: "Given there's no local IB school, is an online tutor really a fair substitute?", answer: "For Nagercoil the comparison is somewhat academic, since there is no genuinely qualified in-house alternative in the district to weigh an online tutor against. Screen sharing, annotated past papers and saved recordings of worked problems cover nearly everything a family would otherwise be seeking, and the trade-off comes with access to specialists nationwide instead of a handful of local generalists." },
    { question: "What kind of vetting does a tutor go through before meeting my family?", answer: "Each tutor's academic background gets verified, along with how recently and how specifically they have taught the subject and level a family needs, plus a look at how they typically mark against published assessment criteria. That recency check matters more here than in a city with an established local IB or IGCSE teaching base, precisely because Nagercoil has none. Everything else gets settled once you watch the trial lesson yourself." },
    { question: "Is there an ideal age or class to begin IB or IGCSE support from Nagercoil?", answer: "Beginning alongside the course itself, Grade 9 for Cambridge or Edexcel IGCSE and Class 11 for the Diploma, leaves the most runway before internal assessments and predicted grades start piling up together. That said, a student picking things up in the final year can still close meaningful gaps if sessions stay tightly focused on the topics and past papers worth the most marks." },
    { question: "Our child currently studies under the Matriculation Board and wants to move to IGCSE. Is that manageable?", answer: "It happens fairly often, mostly because no Nagercoil school offers both boards under one roof for families to weigh side by side. The harder adjustment is rarely the content itself; it is answering to command words the Matriculation Board rarely tests directly, so building that habit a term ahead of the actual switch tends to pay off." },
    { question: "Can lessons be arranged around evenings or weekends for a family in Nagercoil?", answer: "Weekday evenings once school finishes, plus weekend mornings, are what most local families settle into, and online delivery makes that easy to hold consistently. Sessions shift a little lighter during the wetter monsoon stretches or around Pongal and Navaratri if a household prefers, and slotting in an extra class before mocks needs nothing more than a quick message to us." },
    { question: "What if my child and the assigned tutor just don't get along?", answer: "Let us know and a replacement gets arranged. Regular check-ins exist specifically to catch a poor fit early, rather than leaving a child to push through with the wrong tutor for months. There is no lock-in contract behind any of this, so swapping tutors or taking a break from sessions costs nothing." },
    { question: "Does IB Gram have any formal tie to a Nagercoil school, Cambridge or the IB itself?", answer: "No, none whatsoever. IB Gram works independently of every institution named across this page and of the IB Organization, Cambridge Assessment International Education and Pearson Edexcel. Those names only appear here to explain how education actually works around Nagercoil, and a tutor simply teaches to whichever programme or board a family's child already follows." },
  ],

